                    <i class="fas fa-microchip text-3xl text-white"></i>
                </div>
                <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-400 to-blue-400 bg-clip-text text-transparent">
                    Advanced Parallel Computing
                </h1>
                <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-gray-300 mb-8">
                    OpenMP, MPI & OpenCL: Mastering the Complete Parallel Programming Ecosystem
                </p>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
                    <span class="bg-purple-600 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold">OpenMP</span>
                    <span class="bg-blue-600 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold">MPI</span>
                    <span class="bg-indigo-600 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold">OpenCL</span>
                    <span class="bg-green-600 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold">C Programming</span>
                    <span class="bg-yellow-600 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold">GPU Computing</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Project Overview -->
    <section class="py-16">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
            <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center mb-16">
                    <div>
                        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-6">Project Overview</h2>
                        <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 mb-6">
                            This comprehensive parallel computing specialization demonstrates mastery across three fundamental paradigms of high-performance computing through the COMP3221 Parallel Computation module at the University of Leeds.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 mb-6">
                            Each coursework builds upon previous concepts, creating a complete understanding of parallel programming from shared memory systems to distributed clusters and GPU acceleration.
                        </p>
                        <div class="bg-yellow-900/30 border border-yellow-500/50 rounded-lg p-4">
                            <p class="text-yellow-200 text-sm">
                                <i class="fas fa-info-circle mr-2"></i>
                                <strong>Academic Context:</strong> Due to a long-term illness during this period, the implementations represent focused effort on core parallel computing concepts rather than extensive feature development.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border border-gray-700">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-purple-400 mb-4">Technical Achievements</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-3">
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <i class="fas fa-check-circle text-green-400 mt-1 mr-3"></i>
                                <span class="text-gray-300">Implemented parallel Game of Life with OpenMP directives</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <i class="fas fa-check-circle text-green-400 mt-1 mr-3"></i>
                                <span class="text-gray-300">Achieved 3.09x speedup in distributed MPI applications</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <i class="fas fa-check-circle text-green-400 mt-1 mr-3"></i>
                                <span class="text-gray-300">Developed GPU-accelerated heat equation solvers</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <i class="fas fa-check-circle text-green-400 mt-1 mr-3"></i>
                                <span class="text-gray-300">Mastered data dependencies and race condition handling</span>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Three Courseworks -->
    <section class="py-16 bg-gray-800">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
            <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
                <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold text-center text-white mb-16">Three Parallel Computing Paradigms</h2>

                <!-- Coursework 1: OpenMP -->
                <div class="mb-16">
                    <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-8 border border-purple-500/30">
                        <div class="flex items-center mb-6">
                            <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-500 to-purple-600 rounded-full p-3 mr-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-memory text-white text-xl"></i>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-purple-400">Coursework 1: OpenMP Programming</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-400">Shared Memory Parallelization</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                            <div>
                                <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Conway's Game of Life Implementation</h4>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
                                    Parallelized the classic cellular automaton using OpenMP directives, implementing four key parallel functions with proper handling of data dependencies and race conditions.
                                </p>
                                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-400">
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-code text-purple-400 mr-2"></i>283 lines of optimized C code</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-cog text-purple-400 mr-2"></i>4 parallel functions implemented</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-sync text-purple-400 mr-2"></i>Red-black pattern for modified rules</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-shield-alt text-purple-400 mr-2"></i>Thread-safe random generation</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Technical Implementation</h4>
                                <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-sm">
                                    <div class="text-purple-400 mb-2">Key Functions Parallelized:</div>
                                    <div class="text-gray-300 space-y-1">
                                        <div>• numCells() - Cell counting with reduction</div>
                                        <div>• initialiseGrid() - Parallel initialization</div>
                                        <div>• iterateWithOriginalRules() - Moore neighborhood</div>
                                        <div>• iterateWithModifiedRules() - von Neumann + red-black</div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Coursework 2: MPI -->
                <div class="mb-16">
                    <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-8 border border-blue-500/30">
                        <div class="flex items-center mb-6">
                            <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-blue-600 rounded-full p-3 mr-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-network-wired text-white text-xl"></i>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-400">Coursework 2: MPI Programming</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-400">Distributed Message Passing</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                            <div>
                                <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Scalable Distributed Computing</h4>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
                                    Developed MPI applications with comprehensive performance analysis across multiple machines, demonstrating understanding of distributed computing challenges and optimization strategies.
                                </p>
                                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-400">
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-code text-blue-400 mr-2"></i>199 lines of MPI C implementation</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-server text-blue-400 mr-2"></i>Multi-machine cluster deployment</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-chart-line text-blue-400 mr-2"></i>Rigorous performance benchmarking</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-balance-scale text-blue-400 mr-2"></i>Scalability analysis up to 32 processes</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Performance Results</h4>
                                <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-4">
                                    <div class="text-blue-400 mb-3 font-semibold">Speedup Analysis:</div>
                                    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                                        <div class="flex justify-between text-gray-300">
                                            <span>1 process:</span>
                                            <span class="text-green-400">1.00x (baseline)</span>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="flex justify-between text-gray-300">
                                            <span>2 processes:</span>
                                            <span class="text-green-400">1.42x speedup</span>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="flex justify-between text-gray-300">
                                            <span>4 processes:</span>
                                            <span class="text-green-400">1.74x speedup</span>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="flex justify-between text-gray-300">
                                            <span>8 processes:</span>
                                            <span class="text-green-400">3.09x speedup</span>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-2">
                                            Performance degradation at 16+ processes due to network overhead and oversubscription
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Coursework 3: OpenCL -->
                <div class="mb-16">
